  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The possible values of principal quantum number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> can be any positive integer.</p><p>For a particular value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>, the possible values of azimuthal quantum number is from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Thus, for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, the possible <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;values are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>The possible values of magnetic quantum number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> is from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>.</p><p>Thus, for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, the possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>The possible values of spin quantum number&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>In option C.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;not possible for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
